preConditionHook:
// The prior bar left a micro gap -- its low above the high of the bar before
// it -- and this bar pulls back to the gap's lower edge, the with-trend limit
// entry at the breakout point. The limit sits at the high of the bar BEFORE
// the breakout bar (high[2]), which is the indexing the clearer of the two
// sources states; the other writes high[1], contradicting its own quote.
//
// entryOffsetPoints is in PRICE POINTS, not ticks: MinMove and PriceScale are
// UNKNOWN in the feature register and the engine exposes no tick size to
// strategies at all, so the source's one-tick tolerance cannot be written.
// The default 0 is the exact-touch reading; the input widens it where the
// symbol's tick makes that too strict.
//
// A bar's own low reaching a level is not the same as a limit order filling
// there -- the engine fills at the next bar's open -- so this is the price
// TEST, and the fill is the pane's business.
